'''The Invisible Cat''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] that can be obtained from the [[June Bride of the Devil (Event Gacha)|June Bride of the Devil]] event capsule. It was added in [[Version 15.4 Update|Version 15.4]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 863
|rarity = EX
|name1 = The Invisible Cat
|name2 = Groom Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Groom Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
The main advantage of Groom Cat is his standing range, which lets him comfortably engage a sizeable portion of Zombies from a safe distance, including even [[Lord Gravey]]. He isn't hindered by Single Attack or terrible mobility/survivability either, making him somewhat of a rarity as one of the only competent anti-Zombie midrangers in the game, usable even in {{4c}} settings where the likes of [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] are unavailable.

Against Angels, he's superb in the early-midgame where many counters aren't so readily available to the player. He cuts through [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]], [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s, and [[Boraphim]]s like a knife through butter with his 5,128 DPS against targets at Lv.30 (8,145 at Lv.50), assuming [[Fruit Treasures]] are collected. In this niche he is outclassed later by [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]], [[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]], and/or [[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cat]], which are better at dishing out damage.

Even then, he remains a great pick for Zombies, providing certain advantages that [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] can only dream of. Consider boosting him if you can; this gentleman is worth more than a hand in marriage!

